WEBVTT

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:39.990
I've been waiting for this moment, Yabuki Joe!

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.040
Ever since I, the rookie of the year,

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.820
fell victim to your Cross Counter,

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.560
I've battled through my humiliation, just waiting for this moment.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:55.010
Now it's time to show you my Anti-Cross Counter!

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:05.980
Thanks!

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.740
You did it!

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.950
Joe!

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.370
A-And it's Y-Yabuki! Yabuki has collapsed!

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.240
Yabuki's down!

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.470
I did it! I did it, Coach!

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.390
A-All right! It worked!

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:22.530
Way to go!

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.320
You beat the Cross Counter!

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.480
Hooray!

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.480
Hooray!!

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.380
What's going on? I thought the Cross Counter connected!

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.130
Why was it Yabuki who collapsed!?

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:36.670
Joe!

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:37.800
Bro Joe!

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.670
Go to a neutral corner!

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.880
O-Oh no!

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.640
Joe! Get up!

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.600
Get up! Joe, get up!

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.600
Rikiishi-kun!

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.670
Joe! Joe!

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.100
Joe!

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:20.490
Joe! Didn't you say you were going to settle things with me!?

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.110
Get up! Get up!

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:24.980
Joe!

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:25.850
Hey, you!

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:25.860
<i>Joe!</i>

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.000
Hey! You're a professional! Don't be so foolish!

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:28.780
Go back to your seat!

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.620
J-Joe! J-Joe!

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.100
Joe!

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:38.430
Joe! Joe!

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.350
Joe!

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:44.740
Joe...

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.730
Joe!

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.270
He got up!

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.770
H-He's back up! Yabuki got back up on the nine count!

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:46.480
Even after he was floored by the Anti-Cross Counter, he got up!?

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.860
Wh-What a lunatic!

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:49.280
Damn.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.290
Yeah! Go, Bro!

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:55.290
We're with you! Don't go losin' now!

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.290
Fight!

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.800
Now to finish you off!

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.040
Stop! Stop!

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:43.170
Dammit, that little...

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.760
Now, now, Yabuki-kun.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:59.560
Here. Your brain's addled. Your corner's over there.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:11.080
Saved by the bell. What a lucky bastard.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.420
This match is starting to become truly terrifying!

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.800
Yabuki is now drenched 
head-to-toe in his own blood!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:26.000
But, why do you suppose Yabuki's signature move, the Cross Counter, resulted in him hitting the mat?

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.650
I-I wish I knew myself...

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.590
Well, let's play it back in slow motion!

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:39.150
Here, Wolf is going to town on Yabuki, who's using his No Guard stance.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:41.020
He really showered him with blows.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:43.520
Oh, Wolf... Wolf...

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.460
lowers his hips!

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:50.700
Now, this is where he throws the straight left!

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:59.390
Yabuki, who's been waiting for this straight left, throws the Cross.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:05.060
Up until now, Yabuki's Cross has always dominated...

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:06.750
Oh, look at that!

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:07.920
Look at Wolf's left!

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:09.590
There it is!

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.680
Wolf's left looks like it's heading straight for Yabuki's jaw...

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.220
...but then it angles back, 
deflecting Yabuki's counter!

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:21.030
Then, after that...

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.570
Th-This is it!

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.270
What a fearsome anti-counter!

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:36.050
Wolf threw a straight right faster than the eye could register!

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:40.070
Wolf's amazing technique has only now been revealed by this slow motion replay!

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:44.410
He made it look like he'd throw a straight left, only to bend it into an L-shape,

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:47.330
deflecting Yabuki's cross.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.340
That's right.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.310
And on top of that, even though he'd thrown left hooks up to this point,

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:54.850
this was the first straight left he'd thrown, which would have invited the Cross Counter.

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:58.870
I see. So, he gave Yabuki only one chance.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:01.350
Which means he forced him into his trap.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.660
I didn't even see Wolf's straight right!

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.320
Neither did I! Isn't that something!?

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:14.640
At any rate, the slow motion replay has captured the full terror of Wolf's Anti-Cross Counter.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:18.010
You could say that the third round was where the wild brawler Yabuki Joe...{have my reservations with this line but finding hard to fixedit}

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:22.870
was overwhelmed technically by the precision machine that is Wolf Kanagushi.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:25.670
Wolf! Great move!

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:28.180
That's our Wolf!

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.390
What's the matter, Tange-kun?

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:40.110
You're looking pretty serious over there!

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:42.140
Cheer up, will ya?

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:49.380
Now, let me give you a friendly warning as a fellow coach:

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:52.650
Yabuki-kun's getting better and better all the time as a fighter.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:57.300
You should throw in the towel 
before he dies of blunt trauma!

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.170
Seconds out!

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:06.190
Well, whether you forfeit or not, it doesn't look like he's gonna be able to fight in that condition!

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:30.130
Okay, do it! Cave his head in, Wolf!

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:40.480
And so, the fourth round begins!

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.950
Wolf and Yabuki have come out of their respective corners!

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.540
Yabuki!

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.150
Go for it, Yabuki!

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.640
Wolf! Hurry up and beat him!

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.580
Joe...

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:15.150
At the very least, you got back up.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.040
The brawler who defies logic...

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.210
The killer who makes the impossible possible...

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.730
The wild man, Yabuki Joe...

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:23.110
You've been called a lot of things.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:26.280
But, is that just media hype...

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.440
or is that who you really are?

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:29.400
Joe...

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:33.090
This round will answer that.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.820
With Yabuki having taken considerable damage...

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:01.610
we thought Wolf would just finish the fight off straight from the bell.

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:05.460
But Yabuki's legs look like they're about to buckle.

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:08.120
It looks like standing is all he can manage.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.420
He's not attacking yet!

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:13.710
It looks like he's toying with him, deciding which direction to attack from!

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.820
How about I throw another straight left for you now?

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.210
You did it!

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.090
Wolf's Anti-Cross Counter connects again!

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.210
Yabuki's down!

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:05.280
He repeats the Cross Counter from the No Guard stance, even though it's already been countered!

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:08.170
Has Yabuki lost his ability to think?

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.910
Is he immortal?

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.840
Yabuki's up on the count of nine again!{i wanna use nine count but not sure if this is correct boxing terminology}

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:49.470
That idiot had me worried!

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:52.930
Go for it, Bro!

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.290
The match is back on!

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:57.390
Fight!

00:13:58.280 --> 00:13:59.330
Damn...

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.530
Time for another left!

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:21.840
He did it!

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.570
Yeah! Nice one, Bro!

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:40.770
Go to a neutral corner.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:43.900
Yabuki's down again! This is his second fall this round alone!

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.420
I-I can't watch this anymore.

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.050
This isn't even a match now!

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:49.670
It's torture!

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:14.010
O-Oh my god...

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:40.400
Fight!

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:45.840
Hey, Ref! Are you really gonna let this match go on!?

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.840
Stop the match! Yabuki's gonna die at this rate!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:52.310
Coach! Hey, Coach! Throw in the towel already!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.300
Throw in the towel! Now!

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:01.010
No.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:03.990
Joe doesn't care about the towel or the referee.

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:05.320
Those eyes...

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:08.470
Those aren't the eyes of a boxer who'd accept a TKO!

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:14.830
Joe...

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:17.650
Hey, Wolf! Stop messing about!

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:19.330
Just beat him up already!

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:22.730
Gotcha.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:26.420
I've been tormenting him for his arrogance up to this point.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.700
But I've had enough now!

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:29.760
This time, I'll really finish you off...

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:31.970
with the straight left you love so much!

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.570
I'll make you taste total and utter defeat...

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:38.270
and there's not a thing you can do about it!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.080
G-Go to a neutral corner.

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:53.520
Doctor! Hurry!

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:02.370
Yabuki Joe wins by KO in the fourth round!

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:04.750
Yabuki...

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:13.250
Joe!

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:17.010
J-Joe!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.740
Joe!

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:23.930
You did well!

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:26.770
You really gave it your all!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:51.720
We know that Yabuki won with a KO that turned the tables,

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:52.990
but what exactly just happened?

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:56.560
L-Let's see... What should we call that?

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:59.090
I-I suppose you could call it the "Triple Cross Counter."

00:19:59.600 --> 00:20:01.090
T-Triple Cross?

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:03.300
Yes! In other words,

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:09.860
when Yabuki threw a punch over Wolf's left from the No Guard stance, that was the Cross Counter.

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:16.660
But then, Wolf bent his left arm to deflect it, and threw a straight right instead.

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:20.130
You could call that the "Double Cross Counter."

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:21.570
I-I see.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:23.680
But after that, you see...

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:28.220
Yabuki went even further beyond Wolf's terrifying Double Cross.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:33.340
He countered Wolf's new finishing move, the straight right.

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:35.670
In other words, a Triple Cross Counter.

00:20:36.730 --> 00:20:37.650
Like this.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:50.450
The average Cross Counter is four times stronger than a normal punch.

00:20:50.450 --> 00:20:52.910
That means, a Double Cross would be eight times more powerful,

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:57.690
and a Triple Cross would have twelve times the force that a normal punch has!

00:20:58.430 --> 00:20:59.690
At any rate,

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:02.970
this match ended in an exchange of counters.

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:05.850
Yabuki Joe has won the battle of the counters!

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:10.400
Yabuki Joe, known as the wild killer, has specialized in an unrefined boxing technique.

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:14.250
But you could say that the frenzied fighting spirit that his wild heart begets...

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:17.520
has broken the precision machine that is Wolf.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.720
I've been doing this job for many years now,

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:29.270
but I've never felt so overwhelmed with such strange, indescribable emotion.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.280
Yabuki-san! Over here!

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:42.320
One more, please!

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:48.410
Yabuki! Well done! Well done!

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:51.410
Way to go, Killer!

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:08.930
It was real.

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:11.730
Let me through!

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:14.480
Let me through!

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:22.780
Joe!

00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:35.090
Joe...

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:38.050
Can you hear me, Joe?

00:22:38.810 --> 00:22:40.830
Can you hear my voice?

00:22:51.790 --> 00:22:52.480
Joe...

00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:55.280
It's my turn next.

00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:41.250
The intense fight is over.

00:23:41.850 --> 00:23:46.290
I secretly planned a vacation for Joe to help him recuperate.

00:23:47.590 --> 00:23:50.160
The bus was filled with the joyful shouts of a vacation.

00:23:50.860 --> 00:23:55.120
Then came the demoralizing news on the radio that Wolf Kanagushi will not be making a comeback.

00:23:56.410 --> 00:23:59.100
Joe is astonished by this unthinkable turn of events!

00:23:59.100 --> 00:24:02.190
Now, for Joe, as he worries about Wolf,

00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:04.000
which way is tomorrow!?
